OL,3,GNEWSACommunity group completes 'first'
OL,4,Ahostile buy-out of eyesore plot in St
OL,5,AAndrews
OL,6,
OL,7,FA community group has completed a
OL,8,Ffirst-of-its-kind hostile buy-out of a
OL,9,Fpatch of overgrown land in St Andrews.
OL,11,FThe group, called Poets' Neuk, wants to
OL,12,Fdevelop what it describes as "an
OL,13,Feyesore plot" in the Fife town into a
OL,14,Fpublic poetry garden dedicated to Mary,
OL,15,FQueen of Scots.
OL,17,FThe landowner, Forthtay Ltd, previously
OL,18,Flost an appeal against the decision of
OL,19,FScottish ministers to back a compulsory
OL,20,Fpurchase bid.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
